IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P2-section-2-gate: what Articles 8 to 15 and Annex IV share: the facts that decide whether Chapter III Section 2 reaches a
-- high-risk AI system on the date asked, and the way the answers of the Articles add up (Article 8(1), the seam S8 the keel
-- takes: "the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2").
-- Part P2 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744.
-- Status (2026-11-17): the readings here are assumed, not ruled; the text is the Publications Office consolidation, a rendering
-- with no legal effect (the as-enacted wording of an amended provision is quoted from the base file).
--
-- How a requirement function of Articles 8 to 15 reads its gate (the three keel seams S1, S14, S15):
--   S1  `Art 113 the provision group applies` for `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3`, with the route, the placement date and Article 111(2)'s saving.
--       Not applicable on the date asked (not yet, saved, or no route): NOTHING (never JUST FALSE: the keel's reading F-111-2-nothing).
--   S14 `Art 2(2)`: a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products meets only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112.
--       The keel's function answers JUST FALSE for Articles 8 to 15 there ("only ... shall apply"): the requirement function answers JUST FALSE.
--   S15 `Art 2(13)`: where it answers JUST TRUE the application of a specific requirement of Articles 9 to 15 "may be limited", and the extent of
--       the limitation is for the delegated acts of Article 2(13) (outside the sources): NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).

§ `The facts that decide whether the Section reaches the system`

-- Three facts about the harmonisation legislation of Annex I, asked once and passed to Article 2(2) and Article 2(13).
-- The fact that Article 2(2) also reads, "the requirements ... have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation", matters
-- only for Articles 57 to 59 and is not read for Articles 8 to 15.
DECLARE `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` HAS
    `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What the gate answers. One constructor for each way a requirement function reacts.
DECLARE `Arts 8 to 15 gate` IS ONE OF
    `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies`
    `Arts 8 to 15 gate not applicable on the date asked`        -- Article 113 and Article 111(2): not yet, saved, or no route: NOTHING
    `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)`                 -- JUST FALSE
    `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)`      -- NOTHING

@ref Art 113, Art 111(2), Art 2(2) and Art 2(13) as the keel reads them (seams S1, S14, S15)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the provision` IS AN `Article reference`
GIVETH A `Arts 8 to 15 gate`
`Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s route) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`))
    THEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate not applicable on the date asked`
    ELSE CONSIDER `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s route) (`the harmonisation facts`'s `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`) FALSE `the provision`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)`
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `Art 2(13) the application of the requirement or obligation may be limited` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s route) `the provision` (`the harmonisation facts`'s `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`) (`the harmonisation facts`'s `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`)
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)`
             OTHERWISE `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies`

§ `How the answers of the requirements add up`

-- A list of the answers of the requirements (each MAYBE BOOLEAN, JUST TRUE "met") and what they come to.
-- JUST FALSE as soon as one requirement is not met (the text says "shall comply"); JUST TRUE when every requirement answered and each is met;
-- otherwise NOTHING (a requirement not answered, or not applicable on the date asked, is not covered).
@ref Art 8(1)
GIVEN `the answers of the requirements` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Arts 8 to 15 all the requirements are met given the answers` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers of the requirements`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall comply with the requirements laid down in this Section"; one requirement is not met
    ELSE IF       (count `the answers of the requirements` GREATER THAN 0)
              AND (all (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of the requirements`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a requirement is not answered, or it does not apply on the date asked
